  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607184600: Bounded database frame component over verified TLS

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Decision

Lift the database provider above raw transport with a generic bounded frame
contract. `db-exchange` writes a four-byte unsigned big-endian payload length,
writes the payload, performs bounded multi-read assembly, and accepts a reply
only when its declared frame length fits within the received bytes. Consumer
and provider are separately compiled `.kotoba` components and retain separate
high-level database and lower transport/TLS HostCaps.

A real integration test links the Kotoba database consumer to the Kotoba frame
provider and exchanges a length-prefixed ping/pong frame through the native
verified TLS provider. No socket, descriptor, root secret or TLS switch enters
either component.

## Maturity boundary

This is a reusable framing layer, not a claim of PostgreSQL, MySQL or another
specific database wire protocol. Product-specific startup, authentication,
transaction, cancellation and error semantics remain pending and require a
separate narrowed provider/profile.
")))
